From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:09:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmgr-pwrstate: Keep wakeup-path domains on
 in system sleep

At the end of system suspend genpd powers a PMGR domain off once every
device in it has suspended, even a device that put itself on the wakeup
path to stay powered. A USB device controller that keeps its bus session
over suspend-to-idle loses it that way: its controller and PHY domains
go off, the host sees a disconnect and enumerates the device again after
the wake.

Set GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP, so that a domain stays on over system
sleep while a device in it is on the wakeup path. Runtime PM is not
affected. Wake-enabled devices keep their domains on as well; on the
iPad 5 that is i2c0, the bus of the PMU whose charger and RTC wake the
system.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Link: https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard/pull/231#issuecomment-7138590680
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
index 65dc32d30..2a03318b2 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmgr-pwrstate.c
@@ -308,7 +308,12 @@ static int apple_pmgr_ps_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	clock_only = of_property_read_bool(node, "apple,clock-gate-only");
 	if (!clock_only) {
-		ps->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_IRQ_SAFE;
+		/*
+		 * A domain stays on over system sleep while a device in it is
+		 * on the wakeup path, e.g. a USB device controller that keeps
+		 * its bus session over suspend-to-idle.
+		 */
+		ps->genpd.flags |= GENPD_FLAG_IRQ_SAFE | GENPD_FLAG_ACTIVE_WAKEUP;
 		ps->genpd.name = name;
 		ps->genpd.power_on = apple_pmgr_ps_power_on;
 		ps->genpd.power_off = apple_pmgr_ps_power_off;
